 "C0": {
  "code": "INELIG",
  "loc": "Abstract, p.1; Section 2 Preliminaries, p.3",
  "quote": "a \u201cmap of elections\u201d that visualizes a set of 800 elections",
  "note": "The main object is the space of preference profiles (elections), the positionwise distance between them, and statistical cultures for generating synthetic data. The paper studies no aggregation rule or its strategic or computational aspects; Borda scores appear only as a preprocessing step for selecting candidates. Borderline case (elections are inputs to voting rules), but under a strict reading of C0 it is coded INELIG."
